    (0, None, '\'Kostya, quickly speak, what is the matter!\' "V chyom delo", literally "in what is the matter", is a phrase you\'ve heard a few times now. "Govori" is "speak", said to one person. Vika is done with polite questions.'),
    (1, None, '\'Vika, please, stop scaring me!\' "Perestan" is "stop", said to one person. "Pugat", "to scare", is the same family as "ispugalsya", "got scared". Kostya begs.'),
    (2, None, '\'Or I will transfer Nastya to another shift!\' "Perevedu", "I will transfer", has pere-, "across", on the front. Nastya becomes "Nastyu", because she\'s the one being moved. "V druguyu smenu" is "to another shift".'),
