    (4, None, '\'I am listening attentively to your confession.\' "Priznanie", "confession", comes from "priznatsya", the "priznalas" Barinov used about Vika. "Vnimatelno" is "attentively". Her tone is formal and dry.'),
    (5, None, '\'Max found out your secret from Alisa.\' "Uznal", "found out", can also mean "recognised". "Ot Alisy" is "from Alisa": after "ot", Alisa becomes "Alisy". "Sekret" is easy.'),
    (6, None, '\'What secret did that fool find out?\' "Kakoy eshchyo sekret" is "what still secret", "what other secret". "Durak" is "fool", blunt, though Vika says it with some affection.'),
